=> for vmax >= ~37, the lower bound (6/7)meas(G_C)-r/(7vmax) already EXCEEDS 1/1260
   for every core, so a 13-set with L<1/1260 cannot have its perturbing element
   beyond a bounded range. This is the rigorous core of the compactness lemma
   FOR SINGLE perturbations. The GAP: extending to all 13-sets (not just
   single-element perturbations of a tight core) requires bounding meas(G_C)
   from below for ALL 12-subsets C that could appear, which is the open piece.

Smallest theta such that L<theta forces vmax bounded:
  min decoupling floor = 1/143 = 6.993007e-03 (=1/143, at e=6)
  So: L < 1/143 + single-perturbation structure => vmax bounded.
  And the OBSERVED min positive L = 1/1260 < 1/143, consistent.
